SWEET WLAN stage 3 run E (patch 0154, docs/research/37 s.6 step 4 and s.7), boot-arg sweetwlan=7 (= run D of 0132, then rows W15..W17; levels 1-6 behave as before).
W15: the image, its pinned identity and the reset vector at backplane 0 are checked again, then the CA7 wrapper gets the _ai_core_reset of W4 (RESET_CTL 1, IOCTL 0x3, RESET_CTL 0, IOCTL 0x1 = CPUHALT clear) as DHD download_state(FALSE) does (dhd_pcie.c:10343-10346, aiutils.c:1242-1317; brcmfmac resetcore(core, CPUHALT, 0, 0), brcmfmac-chip.c:1357-1358): the firmware runs. Only from the halted state W6 left (IOCTL 0x21).
W16: cfg 0x84 on the tail window, the last RAM word (the length token of W12) read every 50 ms up to 100 times (brcmfmac-pcie.c:113, 1740-1768); a 4-aligned value inside RAM below the last word is the firmware's pciedev_shared_t address, and 16 words there are logged raw (layout: research 37 U13). A timeout is a result, all-ones a stop. cfg 0x84 back at 0.
W17: the CA7 back into reset (RESET_CTL := 1, the CA restore value): the firmware runs at most ~5 s. W16 and W17 arm the CA restore group from their start, so a stop anywhere after the release puts the ARM back into reset.
Pure part (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h): 7 new deny-by-default tuples (run 5), x->done widened to 64 bits (35 tuples), SWW_CPUHALT 0x20, SWW_SH_POLLS/US/WORDS, swl_w15/w16/w17, swl_sh_read.
Glue (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): level 7 accepted; sw3_wr() refuses a CA7 IOCTL store with CPUHALT clear unless the level is 7 and the reset vector store has been made (independent of the tuples).
Final line: "SWEET WLAN: stage 3 level 7 done shared=<hex> reads=<n> words=<n> vars=<n> token=<hex>".
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c rune() (every read failing once and every store failing/dropped/corrupted once: the fake ARM never stays released except a dropped/corrupted W17 store, which the log shows), tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: not yet independently reviewed.

